        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1115183
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-04-04T18:25:16Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "As I understand it, the __traceiter_* functions reflect the raw arguments passed when calling a tracepoint (defined by `TP_PROTO`, e..g. https://android.googlesource.com/kernel/common/+/refs/heads/android13-5.10/include/trace/events/sched.h#140), which is the set of arguments that would be passed to a \"raw tracepoint\" program.\nTime in state uses \"tracepoint\" type programs, which are passed a struct containing the processed fields from the user-visible trace event format (defined by `TP_STRUCT__entry`, e.g. https://android.googlesource.com/kernel/common/+/refs/heads/android13-5.10/include/trace/events/sched.h#146)",
      "parentUuid": "fd8fe8db_2a9969c4",
      "revId": "f1ae03df3323a0e8fc97b47aafb104fe8a9cd1b5",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
